                <pb facs="0984" n="888" sameAs="frus:frus1926v02/pg888"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">853.51/312: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Portugal</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Dearing</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lisbon</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-01-13T19:00:00+00:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 13,
                                1926—7 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received January 14—9
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>3. My 2, January 12. Portuguese Foreign Office has inquired through Dr. Teixeira,
                    who came personally to Legation this afternoon, if possible to have tobacco
                    bonds held by Americans all placed in one bank in America and one bank in
                    London, stating that the Portuguese Government will immediately pay both the
                    principal and the arrears of interest in sterling as soon as this can be done.
                    This arrangement is what the Portuguese Government desires but I do not
                    understand that payment will not be made if this cannot be done. Dr. Teixeira
                    said that he would send me a note this week quoting text of decree which will
                    open necessary credit and stating that the principal and interest of tobacco
                    bonds held by Americans will be paid in sterling or its equivalent. …</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dearing</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
